Subject: ivsc_ace: "switch camera to host failed: -110" on Dell XPS 9320,
 OVTI01A0 never enumerated
To: linux-media@vger.kernel.org

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------q51tuRwPlrzVsixCEIgcklRo
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=flowed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hardware: Dell XPS 13 Plus 9320, BIOS 2.33.0, IPU6 (ADL), IVSC (mei_vsc, 
SPI)
Sensors in ACPI: OVTI01A0 (status 15), OVTI01AB (status 15, on LJCA 
i2c-18), OVTI01AS (status 0)
Kernels tested: 6.12.112 LTS, 7.3 — same result. Camera works under Windows.

Symptoms:
   ivsc_ace intel_vsc-5db76cf6-...: switch camera to host failed: -110
   (reproducible; also on manual rmmod/modprobe ivsc_ace after a clean boot)

ace_get_firmware_id() succeeds, so MEI/VSC transport works, but the
ACE set-camera-owner(HOST) command never gets a response. As a result
acpi_dev_clear_dependencies() is never called, i2c-OVTI01A0:00 is never
created, and the IPU6 media graph has no sensor (libcamera: "No sensor
found for /dev/media0").

ipu_bridge: "Found supported sensor OVTI01A0:00", "Connected 1 cameras".
i2c-OVTI01AB:00: deferred probe pending: ov01a10: waiting for fwnode 
graph endpoint
IVSC firmware: linux-firmware intel/vsc (ivsc_fw, ivsc_pkg_ovti01a0_0, 
ivsc_skucfg_ovti01a0_0_1)
No firmware load errors; no ljca errors.

Full dmesg attached.

Debug trace (dynamic_debug on mei, mei_vsc, mei_vsc_hw, ivsc_ace):
ACE_GET_FW_ID completes normally (10-byte ack at 320.3686).
ACE_SWITCH_CAMERA_TO_HOST (8-byte cmd) is sent at 320.3769, and an
8-byte reply arrives 4 ms later (presumably the ack, since status
must be 0 - otherwise mei_ace_send() would return -EIO). The
subsequent ACE_CMD_RESPONSE event never arrives; the second
wait_for_completion times out at 325.3935 -> -110.
So the IVSC firmware acks the ownership switch but never completes it.
Same symptom as Red Hat bug 2324683 
(https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2324683, XPS 9315, unresolved).

